  "notes": "same_color_as: the two strings denote the same color (compared numerically); serialization: the exact string the specification gives (with fraction_digits when the example states the retained precision). Not transcribed: the example 'oklab(54.0 -25% -5%)' -> 'oklab(0.54 -0.1 -0.02)' in section 16.4 contradicts the normative percent reference range and clamping of section 9.4 (a number L of 54 is clamped to 1).",
  "tolerance": {
   "abs": 5e-05,
   "rationale": "same_color_as pairs where the specification rounds one side (77.78%, 33.33%, 57.28%) differ by up to 5e-5 of the 0-1 sRGB channel (0.005% of 100%); exact pairs agree to about 1e-15. Serialization strings are compared exactly."
  }
 },
